[{"id":"MuU_3.1.1","ref":"3.1.1","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["द्वा सुपर्णा सयुजा सखाया समानं वृक्षं परिषस्वजाते ।","तयोरन्यः पिप्पलं स्वाद्वत्त्यनश्नन्नन्यो अभिचाकशीति ॥ १॥"],"iast":["dvā suparṇā sayujā sakhāyā samānaṃ vṛkṣaṃ pariṣasvajāte ।","tayoranyaḥ pippalaṃ svādvattyanaśnannanyo abhicākaśīti ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Two birds, beautiful of wing, close companions, cling to one common tree: of the two one eats the sweet fruit of the tree, the other eats not but watches his fellow.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 142","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["द्वा","dvā","two (Vedic masculine dual)","dvi"],["सुपर्णा","suparṇā","having beautiful wings","suparṇa"],["सयुजा","sayujā","together","sayuj"],["सखाया","sakhāyā","friends","sakhi"],["समानम्","samānam","same","samāna"],["वृक्षम्","vṛkṣam","tree","vṛkṣa"],["परिषस्वजाते","pariṣasvajāte","embrace","pariṣvaj"],["तयोः","tayoḥ","of those two","tad"],["अन्यः","anyaḥ","one","anya"],["पिप्पलम्","pippalam","fruit","pippala"],["स्वादु","svādu","sweet","svādu"],["अत्ति","atti","eats","ad"],["अन्","an","not","an"],["अश्नन्","aśnan","eating (an-aśnan: not eating)","aś"],["अन्यः","anyaḥ","one","anya"],["अभिचाकशीति","abhicākaśīti","looks on","abhicākaś"]],"tr":{"text":"Two birds that are ever associated and have similar names, cling to the same tree. Of these, one eats the fruit of divergent tastes, and the other looks on without eating.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.1.mp3","whole":[976.55,995.27]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":45,"up":"mundaka","takeaway":"Two birds sit on one tree. One tastes every fruit, sweet and bitter; the other only watches. Both are you."},{"id":"MuU_3.1.2","ref":"3.1.2","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["समाने वृक्षे पुरुषो निमग्नोऽनीशया शोचति मुह्यमानः ।","जुष्टं यदा पश्यत्यन्यमीशमस्य महिमानमिति वीतशोकः ॥ २॥"],"iast":["samāne vṛkṣe puruṣo nimagno’nīśayā śocati muhyamānaḥ ।","juṣṭaṃ yadā paśyatyanyamīśamasya mahimānamiti vītaśokaḥ ॥ 2॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The soul is the bird that sits immersed on the one common tree; but because he is not lord he is bewildered and has sorrow. But when he sees that other who is the Lord and beloved, he knows that all is His greatness and his sorrow passes away from him.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 142","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["समाने","samāne","same","samāna"],["वृक्षे","vṛkṣe","in the tree","vṛkṣa"],["पुरुषः","puruṣaḥ","Person","puruṣa"],["निमग्नः","nimagnaḥ","immersed, absorbed","nimajj"],["अनीशया","anīśayā","through helplessness","anīśā"],["शोचति","śocati","grieves","śuc"],["मुह्यमानः","muhyamānaḥ","bewildered","muh"],["जुष्टम्","juṣṭam","worshipped, revered","juṣ"],["यदा","yadā","when","yadā"],["पश्यति","paśyati","sees","paś"],["अन्यम्","anyam","another","anya"],["ईशम्","īśam","Lord","īśa"],["अस्य","asya","of this","idam"],["महिमानम्","mahimānam","glory","mahiman"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["वीत","vīta","departed","vī"],["शोकः","śokaḥ","sorrow (vīta-śokaḥ: free from sorrow)","śoka"]],"tr":{"text":"On the same tree, the individual soul remains drowned (i.e. stuck), as it were; and so it moans, being worried by its impotence. When it sees thus the other, the adored Lord, and His glory, then it becomes liberated from sorrow.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.2.mp3","whole":[995.27,1014.19]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":46,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.3","ref":"3.1.3","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["यदा पश्यः पश्यते रुक्मवर्णं","कर्तारमीशं पुरुषं ब्रह्मयोनिम् ।","तदा विद्वान् पुण्यपापे विधूय","निरञ्जनः परमं साम्यमुपैति ॥ ३॥"],"iast":["yadā paśyaḥ paśyate rukmavarṇaṃ","kartāramīśaṃ puruṣaṃ brahmayonim ।","tadā vidvān puṇyapāpe vidhūya","nirañjanaḥ paramaṃ sāmyamupaiti ॥ 3॥"],"alt":[{"text":"When, a seer, he sees the Golden-hued, the maker, the Lord, the Spirit who is the source of Brahman, then he becomes the knower and shakes from his wings sin and virtue; pure of all stain he reaches the supreme identity.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 142","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यदा","yadā","when","yadā"],["पश्यः","paśyaḥ","the seer","paśya"],["पश्यते","paśyate","sees","paś"],["रुक्म","rukma","gold (compound member)","rukma"],["वर्णम्","varṇam","colour","varṇa"],["कर्तारम्","kartāram","creator","kartṛ"],["ईशम्","īśam","Lord","īśa"],["पुरुषम्","puruṣam","Person","puruṣa"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["योनिम्","yonim","source","yoni"],["तदा","tadā","then","tadā"],["विद्वान्","vidvān","one who knows","vid"],["पुण्य","puṇya","merit (compound member)","puṇya"],["पापे","pāpe","demerit (puṇya-pāpe: merit and demerit)","pāpa"],["विधूय","vidhūya","having shaken off","vidhū"],["निरञ्जनः","nirañjanaḥ","stainless","nirañjana"],["परमम्","paramam","supreme","parama"],["साम्यम्","sāmyam","equality","sāmya"],["उपैति","upaiti","attains","upe"]],"tr":{"text":"When the seer sees the Purusha – the golden-hued, creator, lord, and the source of the inferior Brahman – then the illumined one completely shakes off both merit and demerit, becomes taintless, and attains absolute equality.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.3.mp3","whole":[1014.19,1033.9]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":47,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.4","ref":"3.1.4","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["प्राणो ह्येष यः सर्वभूतैर्विभाति","विजानन् विद्वान् भवते नातिवादी ।","आत्मक्रीड आत्मरतिः क्रियावानेष ब्रह्मविदां वरिष्ठः ॥ ४॥"],"iast":["prāṇo hyeṣa yaḥ sarvabhūtairvibhāti","vijānan vidvān bhavate nātivādī ।","ātmakrīḍa ātmaratiḥ kriyāvāneṣa brahmavidāṃ variṣṭhaḥ ॥ 4॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This is the life in things that shines manifested by all these beings; a man of knowledge coming wholly to know this, draws back from creeds and too much disputings. In the Self his delight, at play in the Self, doing works, — the best is he among the knowers of the Eternal.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 142","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["भूतैः","bhūtaiḥ","through beings","bhūta"],["विभाति","vibhāti","shines","vibhā"],["विजानन्","vijānan","knowing","vijñā"],["विद्वान्","vidvān","one who knows","vid"],["भवते","bhavate","becomes","bhū"],["न","na","not","na"],["अतिवादी","ativādī","one who speaks beyond","ativādin"],["आत्म","ātma","Self (compound member)","ātman"],["क्रीडः","krīḍaḥ","delighting","krīḍā"],["आत्म","ātma","Self (compound member)","ātman"],["रतिः","ratiḥ","delight (ātma-ratiḥ: delighting in the Self)","rati"],["क्रियावान्","kriyāvān","active in duty","kriyāvat"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["विदाम्","vidām","of knowers (of Brahman)","vid"],["वरिष्ठः","variṣṭhaḥ","the greatest","variṣṭha"]],"tr":{"text":"This one is verily the Vital Force which shines divergently through all beings. Knowing this, the illumined man has no (further) occasion to go beyond anything in his talk. He disports in the Self, delights in the Self, and is engrossed in (spiritual) effort. This one is the chief among the knowers of Brahman.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.4.mp3","whole":[1035.32,1055.83]},"hasBhashya":false,"order":48,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.5","ref":"3.1.5","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["सत्येन लभ्यस्तपसा ह्येष आत्मा","सम्यग्ज्ञानेन ब्रह्मचर्येण नित्यम् ।","अन्तःशरीरे ज्योतिर्मयो हि शुभ्रो","यं पश्यन्ति यतयः क्षीणदोषाः ॥ ५॥"],"iast":["satyena labhyastapasā hyeṣa ātmā","samyagjñānena brahmacaryeṇa nityam ।","antaḥśarīre jyotirmayo hi śubhro","yaṃ paśyanti yatayaḥ kṣīṇadoṣāḥ ॥ 5॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The Self can always be won by truth, by self-discipline, by integral knowledge, by a life of purity, — this Self that is in the inner body, radiant, made all of light whom by the perishing of their blemishes the doers of askesis behold.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 143","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["सत्येन","satyena","by truth","satya"],["लभ्यः","labhyaḥ","attainable","labh"],["तपसा","tapasā","through austerity","tapas"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["एषः","eṣaḥ","this (masculine)","etad"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["सम्यक्","samyak","rightly","samyak"],["ज्ञानेन","jñānena","by knowledge","jñāna"],["ब्रह्मचर्येण","brahmacaryeṇa","through celibacy","brahmacarya"],["नित्यम्","nityam","constantly","nityam"],["अन्तर्","antar","within","antar"],["शरीरे","śarīre","in the body","śarīra"],["ज्योतिः","jyotiḥ","light","jyotis"],["मयः","mayaḥ","consisting of","maya"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["शुभ्रः","śubhraḥ","pure","śubhra"],["यम्","yam","whom","yad"],["पश्यन्ति","paśyanti","they see","paś"],["यतयः","yatayaḥ","seekers","yati"],["क्षीण","kṣīṇa","exhausted","kṣi"],["दोषाः","doṣāḥ","faults (kṣīṇa-doṣāḥ: whose faults have ceased)","doṣa"]],"tr":{"text":"The bright and pure Self within the body, that the monks with (habitual effort and) attenuated blemishes see, is attainable verily through truth, concentration, complete knowledge, and continence, practised constantly.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.5.mp3","whole":[1057.45,1080.08]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":49,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.6","ref":"3.1.6","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["सत्यमेव जयते नानृतं","सत्येन पन्था विततो देवयानः ।","येनाक्रमन्त्यृषयो ह्याप्तकामा","यत्र तत्सत्यस्य परमं निधानम् ॥ ६॥"],"iast":["satyameva jayate nānṛtaṃ","satyena panthā vitato devayānaḥ ।","yenākramantyṛṣayo hyāptakāmā","yatra tatsatyasya paramaṃ nidhānam ॥ 6॥"],"alt":[{"text":"It is Truth that conquers and not falsehood; by Truth was stretched out the path of the journey of the gods, by which the sages winning their desire ascend there where Truth has its supreme abode.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 143","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["जयते","jayate","conquers","ji"],["ना","nā","not","na"],["अनृतम्","anṛtam","falsehood","anṛta"],["सत्येन","satyena","by truth","satya"],["पन्थाः","panthāḥ","path","pathin"],["विततः","vitataḥ","laid out, extended","vitan"],["देव","deva","gods (compound member)","deva"],["यानः","yānaḥ","way","yāna"],["येन","yena","by which","yad"],["आक्रमन्ति","ākramanti","ascend","ākram"],["ऋषयः","ṛṣayaḥ","seers","ṛṣi"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["आप्त","āpta","attained","āp"],["कामाः","kāmāḥ","desires (āpta-kāmāḥ: whose desires are fulfilled)","kāma"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["सत्यस्य","satyasya","of truth","satya"],["परमम्","paramam","supreme","parama"],["निधानम्","nidhānam","treasure, abode","nidhāna"]],"tr":{"text":"Truth alone wins, and not untruth. By truth is laid the path called Devayana, by which the desireless seers ascend to where exists the supreme treasure attainable through truth.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.6.mp3","whole":[1083.25,1103.05]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":50,"up":"mundaka","takeaway":"Truth alone wins in the end, not falsehood. (India's national motto comes from this line.)"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.7","ref":"3.1.7","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["बृहच्च तद्दिव्यमचिन्त्यरूपं","सूक्ष्माच्च तत्सूक्ष्मतरं विभाति ।","दूरात्सुदूरे तदिहान्तिके च","पश्यत्स्विहैव निहितं गुहायाम् ॥ ७॥"],"iast":["bṛhacca taddivyamacintyarūpaṃ","sūkṣmācca tatsūkṣmataraṃ vibhāti ।","dūrātsudūre tadihāntike ca","paśyatsvihaiva nihitaṃ guhāyām ॥ 7॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Vast is That, divine, its form unthinkable; it shines out subtler than the subtle: very far and farther than farness, it is here close to us, for those who have vision it is even here in this world; it is here, hidden in the secret heart.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 143","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["बृहत्","bṛhat","vast","bṛhat"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["दिव्यम्","divyam","divine","divya"],["अचिन्त्य","acintya","unthinkable","acintya"],["रूपम्","rūpam","form","rūpa"],["सूक्ष्मात्","sūkṣmāt","from the subtle","sūkṣma"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["सूक्ष्मतरम्","sūkṣmataram","subtler","sūkṣmatara"],["विभाति","vibhāti","shines","vibhā"],["दूरात्","dūrāt","from afar","dūra"],["सु","su","well","su"],["दूरे","dūre","far away","dūra"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["इह","iha","here","iha"],["अन्तिके","antike","near","antika"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["पश्यत्सु","paśyatsu","in those who see","paś"],["इह","iha","here","iha"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["निहितम्","nihitam","placed, hidden","nidhā"],["गुहायाम्","guhāyām","in the cave","guhā"]],"tr":{"text":"It is great and self-effulgent; and Its form is unthinkable. It is subtler than the subtle. It shines diversely. It is farther away than the far-off, and It is near at hand in this body. Among sentient beings It is (perceived as) seated in this very body, in the cavity of the heart.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.7.mp3","whole":[1104.55,1124.6]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":51,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.8","ref":"3.1.8","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["न चक्षुषा गृह्यते नापि वाचा","नान्यैर्देवैस्तपसा कर्मणा वा ।","ज्ञानप्रसादेन विशुद्धसत्त्वस्ततस्तु तं पश्यते निष्कलं ध्यायमानः ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["na cakṣuṣā gṛhyate nāpi vācā","nānyairdevaistapasā karmaṇā vā ।","jñānaprasādena viśuddhasattvastatastu taṃ paśyate niṣkalaṃ dhyāyamānaḥ ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Eye cannot seize, speech cannot grasp Him, nor these other godheads; not by austerity can he be held nor by works: only when the inner being is purified by a glad serenity of knowledge, then indeed, meditating, one beholds the Spirit indivisible.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 143","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["न","na","not","na"],["चक्षुषा","cakṣuṣā","by sight","cakṣus"],["गृह्यते","gṛhyate","is grasped","grah"],["ना","nā","not","na"],["अपि","api","also","api"],["वाचा","vācā","by speech","vāc"],["ना","nā","not","na"],["अन्यैः","anyaiḥ","by others","anya"],["देवैः","devaiḥ","by the senses, gods","deva"],["तपसा","tapasā","through austerity","tapas"],["कर्मणा","karmaṇā","through ritual","karman"],["वा","vā","or","vā"],["ज्ञान","jñāna","knowledge (compound member)","jñāna"],["प्रसादेन","prasādena","by clarity","prasāda"],["विशुद्ध","viśuddha","purified (compound member)","viśudh"],["सत्त्वः","sattvaḥ","being","sattva"],["ततस्","tatas","then","tatas"],["तु","tu","but","tu"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["पश्यते","paśyate","sees","paś"],["निष्कलम्","niṣkalam","without parts","niṣkala"],["ध्यायमानः","dhyāyamānaḥ","contemplating","dhyā"]],"tr":{"text":"It is not comprehended through the eye, nor through speech, nor through the other senses; nor is It attained through austerity or karma. Since one becomes purified in mind through the favourableness of the intellect, therefore can one see that indivisible Self through meditation.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.8.mp3","whole":[1124.6,1145.73]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":52,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.9","ref":"3.1.9","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["एषोऽणुरात्मा चेतसा वेदितव्यो","यस्मिन्प्राणः पञ्चधा संविवेश ।","प्राणैश्चित्तं सर्वमोतं प्रजानां","यस्मिन्विशुद्धे विभवत्येष आत्मा ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["eṣo’ṇurātmā cetasā veditavyo","yasminprāṇaḥ pañcadhā saṃviveśa ।","prāṇaiścittaṃ sarvamotaṃ prajānāṃ","yasminviśuddhe vibhavatyeṣa ātmā ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This Self is subtle and has to be known by a thought-mind into which the life-force has made its fivefold entry: all the conscious heart of creatures is shot through and inwoven with the currents of the life-force and only when it is purified can this Self manifest its power.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, pp. 143, 144","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["एषः","eṣaḥ","this (masculine)","etad"],["अणुः","aṇuḥ","minute, subtle","aṇu"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["चेतसा","cetasā","by the intellect, mind","cetas"],["वेदितव्यः","veditavyaḥ","should be understood","vid"],["यस्मिन्","yasmin","in which","yad"],["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["पञ्चधा","pañcadhā","fivefold","pañcadhā"],["संविवेश","saṃviveśa","enters","saṃviś"],["प्राणैः","prāṇaiḥ","with the life-breaths","prāṇa"],["चित्तम्","cittam","mind","citta"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarva"],["ओतम्","otam","woven, interwoven","āve"],["प्रजानाम्","prajānām","of creatures","prajā"],["यस्मिन्","yasmin","in which","yad"],["विशुद्धे","viśuddhe","when purified","viśudh"],["विभवति","vibhavati","shines forth","vibhū"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"]],"tr":{"text":"Within (the heart in) the body, where the vital force has entered in five forms, is this subtle Self to be realized through that intelligence by which is pervaded the entire mind as well as the motor and sensory organs of all creatures. And It is to be known in the mind, which having become purified, this Self reveals Itself distinctly.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.9.mp3","whole":[1148.44,1169.36]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":53,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.1.10","ref":"3.1.10","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 1","sa":["यं यं लोकं मनसा संविभाति","विशुद्धसत्त्वः कामयते यांश्च कामान् ।","तं तं लोकं जयते तांश्च कामांस्तस्मादात्मज्ञं ह्यर्चयेद्भूतिकामः ॥ १०॥"],"iast":["yaṃ yaṃ lokaṃ manasā saṃvibhāti","viśuddhasattvaḥ kāmayate yāṃśca kāmān ।","taṃ taṃ lokaṃ jayate tāṃśca kāmāṃstasmādātmajñaṃ hyarcayedbhūtikāmaḥ ॥ 10॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Whatever world the man whose inner being is purified sheds the light of his mind upon, and whatsoever desires he cherishes, that world he takes by conquest, and those desires. Then, let whosoever seeks for success and well-being approach with homage a self-knower.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 144","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यम्","yam","whichever (repeated: whatever)","yad"],["यम्","yam","whichever (repeated: whatever)","yad"],["लोकम्","lokam","world","loka"],["मनसा","manasā","with the mind","manas"],["संविभाति","saṃvibhāti","envisions, manifests","saṃvibhā"],["विशुद्ध","viśuddha","purified (compound member)","viśudh"],["सत्त्वः","sattvaḥ","being","sattva"],["कामयते","kāmayate","desires","kāmay"],["यान्","yān","whichever (desires)","yad"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["कामान्","kāmān","desires","kāma"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["लोकम्","lokam","world","loka"],["जयते","jayate","conquers","ji"],["तान्","tān","them","tad"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["कामान्","kāmān","desires","kāma"],["तस्मात्","tasmāt","from that","tasmāt"],["आत्म","ātma","Self (compound member)","ātman"],["ज्ञम्","jñam","knowing (ātma-jñam: the knower of the Self)","jña"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अर्चयेत्","arcayet","should worship","arcay"],["भूति","bhūti","prosperity","bhūti"],["कामः","kāmaḥ","desiring (bhūti-kāmaḥ: seeking well-being)","kāma"]],"tr":{"text":"The man of pure mind wins those worlds which he mentally wishes for and those enjoyable things which he covets. Therefore one, desirous of prosperity, should adore the knower of the Self.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.1.10.mp3","whole":[1170.61,1194.24]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":54,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.1","ref":"3.2.1","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["स वेदैतत्परमं ब्रह्म धाम","यत्र विश्वं निहितं भाति शुभ्रम् ।","उपासते पुरुषं ये ह्यकामास्ते","शुक्रमेतदतिवर्तन्ति धीराः ॥ १॥"],"iast":["sa vedaitatparamaṃ brahma dhāma","yatra viśvaṃ nihitaṃ bhāti śubhram ।","upāsate puruṣaṃ ye hyakāmāste","śukrametadativartanti dhīrāḥ ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He knows this supreme Brahman as the highest abiding place in which shines out, inset, the radiant world. The wise who are without desire and worship the Spirit pass beyond this sperm.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 144","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["स","sa","he","tad"],["वेद","veda","knows","vid"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["परमम्","paramam","supreme","parama"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["धाम","dhāma","abode","dhāman"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["विश्वम्","viśvam","all","viśva"],["निहितम्","nihitam","lodged","nidhā"],["भाति","bhāti","shines","bhā"],["शुभ्रम्","śubhram","pure","śubhra"],["उपासते","upāsate","worship","upās"],["पुरुषम्","puruṣam","Person","puruṣa"],["ये","ye","who","yad"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अकामाः","akāmāḥ","free from desires","akāma"],["ते","te","they","tad"],["शुक्रम्","śukram","pure","śukra"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["अतिवर्तन्ति","ativartanti","transcend","ativṛt"],["धीराः","dhīrāḥ","the discerning","dhīra"]],"tr":{"text":"He knows this supreme abode, this Brahman, in which is placed the Universe and which shines holy. Those wise ones indeed, who having become desireless, worship this (enlightened) person, transcend this human seed.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.1.mp3","whole":[1195.66,1216.38]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":55,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.2","ref":"3.2.2","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["कामान् यः कामयते मन्यमानः","स कामभिर्जायते तत्र तत्र ।","पर्याप्तकामस्य कृतात्मनस्तु","इहैव सर्वे प्रविलीयन्ति कामाः ॥ २॥"],"iast":["kāmān yaḥ kāmayate manyamānaḥ","sa kāmabhirjāyate tatra tatra ।","paryāptakāmasya kṛtātmanastu","ihaiva sarve pravilīyanti kāmāḥ ॥ 2॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He who cherishes desires and his mind dwells with his longings, is by his desires born again wherever they lead him, but the man who has won all his desire and has found his soul, for him even here in this world vanish away all desires.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 144","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["कामान्","kāmān","desires","kāma"],["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["कामयते","kāmayate","desires","kāmay"],["मन्यमानः","manyamānaḥ","thinking, believing","man"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["कामभिः","kāmabhiḥ","by desires","kāma"],["जायते","jāyate","is born","jan"],["तत्र","tatra","there","tatra"],["तत्र","tatra","there","tatra"],["पर्याप्त","paryāpta","fulfilled","paryāp"],["कामस्य","kāmasya","of desires (paryāpta-kāmasya: of one whose desires are fulfilled)","kāma"],["कृतात्मनः","kṛtātmanaḥ","of one with a disciplined self","kṛtātman"],["तु","tu","but","tu"],["इह","iha","here","iha"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["सर्वे","sarve","all","sarva"],["प्रविलीयन्ति","pravilīyanti","dissolve","pravilī"],["कामाः","kāmāḥ","desires","kāma"]],"tr":{"text":"He who covets the desirable things, while brooding (on the virtues), is born amidst those very surroundings along with the desires. But for one who has got his wishes fulfilled and who is Selfpoised, all the longings vanish even here.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.2.mp3","whole":[1217.67,1237.34]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":56,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.3","ref":"3.2.3","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["नायमात्मा प्रवचनेन लभ्यो","न मेधया न बहुना श्रुतेन ।","यमेवैष वृणुते तेन लभ्यस्तस्यैष आत्मा विवृणुते तनूं स्वाम् ॥ ३॥"],"iast":["nāyamātmā pravacanena labhyo","na medhayā na bahunā śrutena ।","yamevaiṣa vṛṇute tena labhyastasyaiṣa ātmā vivṛṇute tanūṃ svām ॥ 3॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This Self is not won by exegesis, nor by brain-power, nor by much learning of Scripture. Only by him whom It chooses can It be won; to him this Self unveils its own body.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 145","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["न","na","not","na"],["अयम्","ayam","this (masculine)","idam"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["प्रवचनेन","pravacanena","by discourse","pravacana"],["लभ्यः","labhyaḥ","attainable","labh"],["न","na","not","na"],["मेधया","medhayā","by intellect","medhā"],["न","na","not","na"],["बहुना","bahunā","by much","bahu"],["श्रुतेन","śrutena","by learning","śruta"],["यम्","yam","whom","yad"],["एवा","evā","indeed","eva"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["वृणुते","vṛṇute","chooses","vṛ"],["तेन","tena","by him","tad"],["लभ्यः","labhyaḥ","attainable","labh"],["तस्य","tasya","of that","tad"],["एषः","eṣaḥ","this (masculine)","etad"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["विवृणुते","vivṛṇute","reveals","vivṛ"],["तनूम्","tanūm","own body","tanū"],["स्वाम्","svām","one's own","sva"]],"tr":{"text":"This Self is not attained through study, nor through the intellect, nor through much hearing. The very Self which this one (i.e. the aspirant) seeks is attainable through that fact of seeking; this Self of his reveals Its own nature.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.3.mp3","whole":[1238.63,1257.05]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":57,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.4","ref":"3.2.4","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["नायमात्मा बलहीनेन लभ्यो","न च प्रमादात्तपसो वाप्यलिङ्गात् ।","एतैरुपायैर्यतते यस्तु विद्वांस्तस्यैष आत्मा विशते ब्रह्मधाम ॥ ४॥"],"iast":["nāyamātmā balahīnena labhyo","na ca pramādāttapaso vāpyaliṅgāt ।","etairupāyairyatate yastu vidvāṃstasyaiṣa ātmā viśate brahmadhāma ॥ 4॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This Self cannot be won by any who is without strength, nor with error in the seeking, nor by an askesis without the true mark: but when a man of knowledge strives by these means his self enters into Brahman, his abiding place.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 145","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["न","na","not","na"],["अयम्","ayam","this (masculine)","idam"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["बल","bala","strength (compound member)","bala"],["हीनेन","hīnena","by one lacking (strength)","hā"],["लभ्यः","labhyaḥ","attained","labh"],["न","na","not","na"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["प्रमादात्","pramādāt","by carelessness","pramāda"],["तपसः","tapasaḥ","by austerity","tapas"],["वा","vā","or","vā"],["अपि","api","also","api"],["अलिङ्गात्","aliṅgāt","without symbols of renunciation","aliṅga"],["एतैः","etaiḥ","by these","etad"],["उपायैः","upāyaiḥ","by these means","upāya"],["यतते","yatate","strives","yat"],["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["तु","tu","but","tu"],["विद्वान्","vidvān","one who knows","vid"],["तस्य","tasya","of that","tad"],["एषः","eṣaḥ","this (masculine)","etad"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["विशते","viśate","enters","viś"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["धाम","dhāma","abode","dhāman"]],"tr":{"text":"This Self is not attained by one devoid of strength, nor through delusion, nor through knowledge unassociated with monasticism. But the Self of that knower, who strives through these means, enters into the abode that is Brahman.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.4.mp3","whole":[1258.26,1279.77]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":58,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.5","ref":"3.2.5","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["संप्राप्यैनमृषयो ज्ञानतृप्ताः","कृतात्मानो वीतरागाः प्रशान्ताः ।","ते सर्वगं सर्वतः प्राप्य धीरा","युक्तात्मानः सर्वमेवाविशन्ति ॥ ५॥"],"iast":["saṃprāpyainamṛṣayo jñānatṛptāḥ","kṛtātmāno vītarāgāḥ praśāntāḥ ।","te sarvagaṃ sarvataḥ prāpya dhīrā","yuktātmānaḥ sarvamevāviśanti ॥ 5॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Attaining to him, seers glad with fullness of knowledge, perfected in the Self, all passions cast from them, tranquillised, — these, the wise, come to the all-pervading from every side, and, uniting themselves with him, enter utterly the All.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 145","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["सम्प्राप्य","samprāpya","having fully attained","samprāp"],["एनम्","enam","this one","enad"],["ऋषयः","ṛṣayaḥ","seers","ṛṣi"],["ज्ञान","jñāna","knowledge (compound member)","jñāna"],["तृप्ताः","tṛptāḥ","satisfied","tṛp"],["कृतात्मानः","kṛtātmānaḥ","disciplined in mind","kṛtātman"],["वीत","vīta","departed","vī"],["रागाः","rāgāḥ","attachments (vīta-rāgāḥ: free from attachment)","rāga"],["प्रशान्ताः","praśāntāḥ","peaceful","praśam"],["ते","te","they","tad"],["सर्वगम्","sarvagam","all-pervading","sarvaga"],["सर्वतस्","sarvatas","on every side","sarvatas"],["प्राप्य","prāpya","having reached","prāp"],["धीराः","dhīrāḥ","the discerning","dhīra"],["युक्त","yukta","united","yuj"],["आत्मानः","ātmānaḥ","selves (yuktātmānaḥ: with selves united)","ātman"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarva"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["आविशन्ति","āviśanti","enter","āviś"]],"tr":{"text":"Having attained this, the seers become contented with their knowledge, established in the Self, freed from attachment, and composed. Having realized the all-pervasive One everywhere, these discriminating people, ever merged in contemplation, enter into the All.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.5.mp3","whole":[1281.4,1303.4]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":59,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.6","ref":"3.2.6","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["वेदान्तविज्ञानसुनिश्चितार्थाः","संन्यासयोगाद्यतयः शुद्धसत्त्वाः ।","ते ब्रह्मलोकेषु परान्तकाले","परामृताः परिमुच्यन्ति सर्वे ॥ ६॥"],"iast":["vedāntavijñānasuniścitārthāḥ","saṃnyāsayogādyatayaḥ śuddhasattvāḥ ।","te brahmalokeṣu parāntakāle","parāmṛtāḥ parimucyanti sarve ॥ 6॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Doers of askesis who have made sure of the aim of the whole-knowledge of Vedanta, the inner being purified by the Yoga of renunciation, all in the hour of their last end passing beyond death are released into the worlds of the Brahman.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 145","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["वेदान्त","vedānta","the end or culmination of the Veda (compound member)","vedānta"],["विज्ञान","vijñāna","knowledge","vijñāna"],["सु","su","well","su"],["निश्चित","niścita","ascertained","niści"],["अर्थाः","arthāḥ","aims","artha"],["संन्यास","saṃnyāsa","renunciation (compound member)","saṃnyāsa"],["योगात्","yogāt","through the discipline","yoga"],["यतयः","yatayaḥ","ascetics","yati"],["शुद्ध","śuddha","pure (compound member)","śudh"],["सत्त्वाः","sattvāḥ","beings","sattva"],["ते","te","they","te"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["लोकेषु","lokeṣu","in the worlds","loka"],["पर","para","supreme","para"],["अन्त","anta","end (compound member)","anta"],["काले","kāle","at the time","kāla"],["परामृताः","parāmṛtāḥ","supreme immortality","parāmṛta"],["परिमुच्यन्ति","parimucyanti","are completely liberated","parimuc"],["सर्वे","sarve","all","sarva"]],"tr":{"text":"Those to whom the entity presented by the Vedantic knowledge has become fully ascertained, who are assiduous and have become pure in mind through the Yoga of monasticism – all of them, at the supreme moment of final departure, become identified with the supreme Immortality in the worlds that are Brahman, and they become freed on every side.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.6.mp3","whole":[1304.65,1325.24]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":60,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.7","ref":"3.2.7","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["गताः कलाः पञ्चदश प्रतिष्ठा","देवाश्च सर्वे प्रतिदेवतासु ।","कर्माणि विज्ञानमयश्च आत्मा","परेऽव्यये सर्वे एकीभवन्ति ॥ ७॥"],"iast":["gatāḥ kalāḥ pañcadaśa pratiṣṭhā","devāśca sarve pratidevatāsu ।","karmāṇi vijñānamayaśca ātmā","pare’vyaye sarve ekībhavanti ॥ 7॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The fifteen parts return into their foundations, and all the gods pass into their proper godheads, works and the Self of Knowledge, — all become one in the Supreme and Imperishable.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 146","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["गताः","gatāḥ","gone","gam"],["कलाः","kalāḥ","parts","kalā"],["पञ्चदश","pañcadaśa","fifteen","pañcadaśan"],["प्रतिष्ठाः","pratiṣṭhāḥ","foundations","pratiṣṭhā"],["देवाः","devāḥ","gods","deva"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सर्वे","sarve","all","sarva"],["प्रतिदेवतासु","pratidevatāsu","in their respective deities","pratidevatā"],["कर्माणि","karmāṇi","works","karman"],["विज्ञान","vijñāna","knowledge","vijñāna"],["मयः","mayaḥ","consisting of","maya"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["परे","pare","in the supreme","para"],["अव्यये","avyaye","imperishable","avyaya"],["सर्वे","sarve","all","sarva"],["एकीभवन्ति","ekībhavanti","become one","ekībhū"]],"tr":{"text":"To their sources repair the fifteen constituents (of the body) and to their respective gods go all the gods (of the senses). The karmas and the soul appearing like the intellect, all become unified with the supreme Undecaying.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.7.mp3","whole":[1325.24,1345.87]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":61,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.8","ref":"3.2.8","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["यथा नद्यः स्यन्दमानाः समुद्रेऽस्तं गच्छन्ति नामरूपे विहाय ।","तथा विद्वान् नामरूपाद्विमुक्तः","परात्परं पुरुषमुपैति दिव्यम् ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["yathā nadyaḥ syandamānāḥ samudre’staṃ gacchanti nāmarūpe vihāya ।","tathā vidvān nāmarūpādvimuktaḥ","parātparaṃ puruṣamupaiti divyam ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"As rivers in their flowing reach their home in the ocean and cast off their names and forms, even so one who knows is delivered from name and form and reaches the Supreme beyond the Most High, even the Divine Person.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 146","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यथा","yathā","as","yathā"],["नद्यः","nadyaḥ","rivers","nadī"],["स्यन्दमानाः","syandamānāḥ","flowing","syand"],["समुद्रे","samudre","in the ocean","samudra"],["अस्तम्","astam","to disappearance","asta"],["गच्छन्ति","gacchanti","go","gam"],["नाम","nāma","name","nāman"],["रूपे","rūpe","form (nāma-rūpe: name and form)","rūpa"],["विहाय","vihāya","abandoning","vihā"],["तथा","tathā","thus","tathā"],["विद्वान्","vidvān","one who knows","vid"],["नाम","nāma","name","nāman"],["रूपात्","rūpāt","from form (nāma-rūpāt: from name and form)","rūpa"],["विमुक्तः","vimuktaḥ","liberated","vimuc"],["परात्","parāt","from the Supreme","para"],["परम्","param","highest","para"],["पुरुषम्","puruṣam","Person","puruṣa"],["उपैति","upaiti","attains","upe"],["दिव्यम्","divyam","divine","divya"]],"tr":{"text":"As rivers, flowing down, become indistinguishable on reaching the sea by giving up their names and forms, so also the illumined soul, having become freed from name and form, reaches the self-effulgent Purusha that is higher than the higher (Maya).","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.8.mp3","whole":[1346.71,1368.96]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":62,"up":"mundaka","takeaway":"Rivers keep their names until they reach the sea. Freedom is losing a smaller identity into a greater one."},{"id":"MuU_3.2.9","ref":"3.2.9","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["स यो ह वै तत्परमं ब्रह्म वेद","ब्रह्मैव भवति नास्याब्रह्मवित्कुले भवति ।","तरति शोकं तरति पाप्मानं गुहाग्रन्थिभ्यो","विमुक्तोऽमृतो भवति ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["sa yo ha vai tatparamaṃ brahma veda","brahmaiva bhavati nāsyābrahmavitkule bhavati ।","tarati śokaṃ tarati pāpmānaṃ guhāgranthibhyo","vimukto’mṛto bhavati ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He, verily, who knows that Supreme Brahman becomes himself Brahman; in his lineage none is born who knows not the Brahman. He crosses beyond sorrow, he crosses beyond sin, he is delivered from the knotted cord of the secret heart and becomes immortal.—","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 146","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["स","sa","he","tad"],["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["ह","ha","indeed","ha"],["वै","vai","indeed","vai"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["परमम्","paramam","supreme","parama"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["वेद","veda","knows","vid"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["भवति","bhavati","becomes","bhū"],["न","na","not","na"],["अस्य","asya","of this","idam"],["अ","a","not","a"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["विद्","vid","knower (a-brahma-vit: one ignorant of Brahman)","vid"],["कुले","kule","in the family","kula"],["भवति","bhavati","becomes","bhū"],["तरति","tarati","crosses","tṛ"],["शोकम्","śokam","sorrow","śoka"],["तरति","tarati","crosses","tṛ"],["पाप्मानम्","pāpmānam","evil","pāpman"],["गुहा","guhā","cave","guhā"],["ग्रन्थिभ्यः","granthibhyaḥ","from the knots","granthi"],["विमुक्तः","vimuktaḥ","liberated","vimuc"],["अमृतः","amṛtaḥ","immortal","amṛta"],["भवति","bhavati","becomes","bhū"]],"tr":{"text":"Anyone who knows that supreme Brahman becomes Brahman indeed. In his line is not born anyone who does not know Brahman. He overcomes grief, and rises above aberrations; and becoming freed from the knots of the heart, he attains immortality.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.9.mp3","whole":[1370.46,1391.8]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":63,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.10","ref":"3.2.10","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["तदेतदृचाऽभ्युक्तम् ।","क्रियावन्तः श्रोत्रिया ब्रह्मनिष्ठाः","स्वयं जुह्वत एकर्षिं श्रद्धयन्तः ।","तेषामेवैतां ब्रह्मविद्यां वदेत","शिरोव्रतं विधिवद्यैस्तु चीर्णम् ॥ १०॥"],"iast":["tadetadṛcā’bhyuktam ।","kriyāvantaḥ śrotriyā brahmaniṣṭhāḥ","svayaṃ juhvata ekarṣiṃ śraddhayantaḥ ।","teṣāmevaitāṃ brahmavidyāṃ vadeta","śirovrataṃ vidhivadyaistu cīrṇam ॥ 10॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This is That declared by the Rig Veda. Doers of works, versed in the Veda, men absorbed in the Brahman, who putting their faith in the sole-seer offer themselves to him sacrifice, — to them one should speak this Brahmanknowledge, men by whom the Vow of the Head has been done according to the rite.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 146","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["ऋचा","ṛcā","by a Rigvedic hymn","ṛc"],["अभ्युक्तम्","abhyuktam","declared","abhivac"],["क्रियावन्तः","kriyāvantaḥ","performers of actions","kriyāvat"],["श्रोत्रियाः","śrotriyāḥ","learned in the Vedas","śrotriya"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["निष्ठाः","niṣṭhāḥ","established","niṣṭhā"],["स्वयम्","svayam","oneself","svayam"],["जुह्वतः","juhvataḥ","offering into the fire","hu"],["एक","eka","one","eka"],["ऋषिम्","ṛṣim","seer (Ekarṣi: the sole-seer sacrificial fire)","ṛṣi"],["श्रद्धयन्तः","śraddhayantaḥ","with faith","śraddhayantaḥ"],["तेषाम्","teṣām","of them","tad"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["एताम्","etām","this","etad"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["विद्याम्","vidyām","knowledge (accusative)","vidyā"],["वदेत","vadeta","one should teach","vad"],["शिरोव्रतम्","śirovratam","the head-vow","śirovrata"],["विधिवत्","vidhivat","properly, according to the rules","vidhivat"],["यैः","yaiḥ","by whom","yad"],["तु","tu","but","tu"],["चीर्णम्","cīrṇam","completed","car"]],"tr":{"text":"This (rule) has been revealed by the mantra (which runs thus): ‘To them alone should one expound this knowledge of b who are engaged in the practice of disciplines, versed in the Vedas, and indeed devoted to Brahman, who personally sacrifice to the fire called Ekarsi with faith, and by whom has been duly accomplished the vow of holding fire on the head.’","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.10.mp3","whole":[1393.43,1421.4]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":64,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_3.2.11","ref":"3.2.11","section":"Muṇḍaka 3 · Section 2","sa":["तदेतत्सत्यमृषिरङ्गिराः","पुरोवाच नैतदचीर्णव्रतोऽधीते ।","नमः परमऋषिभ्यो नमः परमऋषिभ्यः ॥ ११॥"],"iast":["tadetatsatyamṛṣiraṅgirāḥ","purovāca naitadacīrṇavrato’dhīte ।","namaḥ paramaṛṣibhyo namaḥ paramaṛṣibhyaḥ ॥ 11॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This is That, the Truth of things, which the seer Angiras spoke of old. This none learns who has not performed the Vow of the Head. Salutation to the seers supreme! Salutation to the seers supreme!","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 147","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["ऋषिः","ṛṣiḥ","sage","ṛṣi"],["अङ्गिराः","aṅgirāḥ","Angirasa","aṅgiras"],["पुरा","purā","formerly","purā"],["उवाच","uvāca","said","vac"],["न","na","not","na"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["अ","a","not","a"],["चीर्ण","cīrṇa","performed","car"],["व्रतः","vrataḥ","vow","vrata"],["अधीते","adhīte","studies","adhī"],["नमः","namaḥ","salutation","namas"],["परम","parama","supreme (compound member)","parama"],["ऋषिभ्यः","ṛṣibhyaḥ","to the seers","ṛṣi"],["नमः","namaḥ","salutation","namas"],["परम","parama","supreme (compound member)","parama"],["ऋषिभ्यः","ṛṣibhyaḥ","to the seers","ṛṣi"]],"tr":{"text":"The seer Angiras spoke of this Truth in the days of yore. One that has not fulfilled the vow does not read this. Salutation to the great seers. Salutation to the great seers.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.3.2.11.mp3","whole":[1422.94,1442.7]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":65,"up":"mundaka"}]